.TH JALTRIX 1 "2026-11-09" "JALTRIX 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
jaltrix \- JALTRIX independent Snort investigation console
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jaltrix
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Native desktop console by Jan Herrera. Opens with explicitly labeled demonstration
alerts. Snort is a separate program; the graphical interface runs without root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --language es-419|en-US
Select Latin American Spanish or American English.
.TP
.B --log PATH
Import a local Snort alert_json file.
.TP
.B --follow
Follow the file supplied with --log. Independent collection can be enabled
explicitly in the service panel.
.TP
.B --pcap PATH --rules PATH
Validate rules and replay a local PCAP or supported PCAPNG in an isolated profile.
.TP
.B --service
Open managed sensor controls without starting or changing the service.
.TP
.B --about
Show developer and licensing information.
.TP
.B --legal
Show component notices and licenses.
.TP
.B --data-dir PATH
Use a separate data directory, including cases and settings.
.TP
.B --backup PATH.zip
Create a private backup, including online SQLite snapshots. Does not open the GUI.
.TP
.B --restore PATH.zip --data-dir NEW_DIRECTORY
Verify and restore a backup into a new directory. Existing data is never overwritten.
.TP
.B --migrate-system
Migrate the old managed sensor through native administrator authentication.
Preserves rules and running/boot states; see MIGRATION.md.
.SH KEYBOARD
Ctrl+Q closes the desktop window. Ctrl+K focuses search.
Independent sensor and collector services are not stopped when the GUI closes.
.SH FILES
Data defaults to $XDG_DATA_HOME/jaltrix or ~/.local/share/jaltrix.
Demo, replay and live data are separated. Capture service configuration, when
explicitly installed, resides in /etc/jaltrix.
.SH SAFETY
Firewall response is disabled until an administrator configures an allowed-target
policy. Each action requires explicit confirmation and verification. EDR isolation
is disabled without a tested provider. Consult the included security documentation.
